              Station  : Vung Tau-B                Latitude:  10 20.4N
              Country  : Vietnam                  Longitude: 107 04.3E          
              JASL #   : 383B                 Time Meridian: 105E (GMT + 7 hr) 
              GLOSS #  : none Originator #: 383      NODC #: 11100701
              Contributor  : University of Hawaii Sea Level Center (UHSLC)
                             1000 Pope Rd. MSB 317
                             Honolulu, HI 96822
              Originator   : UHSLC in collaboration with
                             Marine Hydro-meteorological Center
                             No. 4 Dang Thai Than Street
                             Hanoi VIETNAM
              Original Data: digital (PRS, RAD, ENC)
              Instrmnt Type: starting 2007:
                             1) radar (RAD) gauge (Vega Vegapuls 62)
                             2) pressure transducer (PRS)
                             3) Handar Encoder 436-A (ENC), float/well

                             Primary channel used in JASL set:
                             2007-2015: RAD
                             2016-2018: ENC
                            *short gaps in primary channel filled with
                             other channels as available; see UHSLC for
                             specific dates
              Digitzd Intvl: 3 min (RAD); 2 min (PRS); 
                             15 min (ENC)
              Present Data : Hourly, daily, and monthly values obtained by:     
                    Hourly : 3-point Hanning Filter centered on the hour
                    Daily  : 119-point convolution filter (Bloomfield, 1976)    
                             centered on noon applied to the hourly data        
                             with respective periods of the 95, 50, and 5%      
                             amplitude points at 124.0, 60.2, and 40.2 hours    
                    Monthly: Simple average of all daily values; calculated if  
                             7 or fewer days are missing                        
              Span of data : 15 Oct 2007 - 31 Dec 2018
              Gaps > 1 mon : none
              Time Refernce: GMT (hours 00-23)   Space-filler Flag   :-9999     
              Units        : millimeters         Missing Data Flag   : 9999     
              Existing     : Yes                 Operational         : yes
              Sat. Trans.  : Yes                 Distribution        : 2007-2018
              Refernce Levl: Heights are referred to the station tide staff 
                             zero, which is linked to land-based benchmarks. 
                             This reference zero is unique to this station and
                             is not an official datum (chart, national, etc.) 
                             and is not relative to local tidal parameters, 
                             such as mean lower low water.  See the Originators
                             for benchmark descriptions, maps, and the geodetic
                             levelling history.
                             383A is separate from 383B since they have
                             unique reference zeros.
              Comment      : The daily  and monthly means reveal no apparent    
                             changes in the reference level. Tidal analysis
                             does not resolve all tidal components thus the
                             residuals have fluctuations.  It is assumed the
                             timing is good.

                             JASL Nov 2019 update replaces 2016- 03 Sep 2017.
                                                                                
